[node name="RichTextLabel" type="RichTextLabel" parent="Camera3D/Interface/HelpWindow/TabContainer/Tips/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer"]
layout_mode = 2
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[center][i]Keeping things organized[/i][/center]
For systems comprised of several subsystems, each with different numbers of layers, it is recommended to assemble these in separate project files. You can use the File>Import Machine option to instantiate saved scenes in a larger project.
Use [color=FF6A00]links[/color] to connect the interfaces of instanced machines, as by default parts of one machine do not not affect parts of another.
Instanced machines cannot be edited freely, unless Edit>Make Local is used. An exception to this is setting [color=00FF97]pins[/color] to be [color=00FFFF]outputs[/color] and their directionality/state. If the \"Store diff\" option in settings is enabled, this data, along with things like modified part positions (for example data stored in memory cells) will be saved in the project file without affecting the instance's source file.
Edit>Clear Diff can be used to reset a machine instance to its original state.

Note: At this time, importing projects that contain multiple machines will not work well."
fit_content = true

